# Calls to the Mini CRM API. Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension,
# Visual Studio and JetBrains IDEs.
# This file only calls our own API. It never contains the tracker API key:
# the backend reads it from .env.

@api = http://localhost:5080/api
# Set this to the id returned by "Create a lead".
@leadId = 1

### Test step 1: tracker connectivity (expect status_code 200 inside the answer)
GET {{api}}/tracker/ping

### Create a lead
POST {{api}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ann Lee",
  "email": "ann@example.com",
  "phone": "+12025550123",
  "source": "facebook",
  "amount": 199.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### List leads. All filters are optional. name, email, phone, source and currency
### match part of the value; status is exact; amount and created are ranges.
### Answer: { items, page, page_size, total_count }. page_size is 1-100 (default 20).
GET {{api}}/leads?status=new&source=face&name=ann&amount_from=100&created_from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&page=1&page_size=20

### Get one lead
GET {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}

### Edit a lead (status can't be changed here)
PUT {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ann Lee",
  "email": "ann@example.com",
  "phone": "+12025550123",
  "source": "google",
  "amount": 249.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Change status (not to converted)
POST {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "contacted" }

### Test step 2: convert (tracker answers 201)
POST {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "converted" }

### Test step 3: convert the same lead again (tracker answers 200 + duplicate:true)
POST {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "converted" }

### Test step 5, part 1: create a NEW lead for the retry test.
### The lead from steps 2-3 was already sent, so the tracker would only answer "duplicate".
POST {{api}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Retry Test",
  "email": "retry.test@example.com",
  "source": "facebook",
  "amount": 99.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Test step 5, part 2: convert the new lead with a simulated 500
### (attempt 1: 500, attempt 2 about 10 s later: 201, same event_id)
# Set this to the id returned by part 1 (2 on a fresh database).
@retryLeadId = 2
POST {{api}}/leads/{{retryLeadId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "converted", "simulate_server_error": true }

### Test step 5, part 3: wait about 10 s, then check both attempts
GET {{api}}/leads/{{retryLeadId}}/events

### The lead's events and every attempt (request + response)
GET {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}/events

### Allowed statuses
GET {{api}}/leads/statuses

### Delete a lead (409 if it has tracker events)
DELETE {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}

### Rule check: a lead with no amount. Converting it gives 409.
POST {{api}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "No Amount", "email": "no.amount@example.com" }

### Validation check: no email and no phone -> 400
POST {{api}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "No Contact" }

### Settings: tracker endpoints and their templates
GET {{api}}/tracker/endpoints

### Settings: the macros templates can use
GET {{api}}/tracker/macros

### Settings: preview templates for a sample lead (nothing is saved; problems are in "errors")
POST {{api}}/tracker/endpoints/2/preview
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url_template": "https://bipro2interface.sseku.com/api/candidate-tracker/conversions",
  "body_template": "{\"event_id\":\"{event_id}\",\"email\":\"{email}\",\"amount\":{amount}}",
  "event_id_template": "conv_{lead_id}"
}

### Settings: rule check, invalid templates -> 400 per field
PUT {{api}}/tracker/endpoints/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url_template": "http://example.com",
  "body_template": "{\"x\":\"{unknown}\"}",
  "event_id_template": "conv_{email}"
}

### Settings: put the purchase templates back to the defaults
POST {{api}}/tracker/endpoints/2/reset

### Lead capture: settings (shows whether the pixel and postback URLs are on, and the token)
GET {{api}}/inbound/settings

### Lead capture: pixel. Paste the token from the settings answer above.
@inboundToken = paste-your-inbound-token
GET {{api}}/inbound/pixel.png?token={{inboundToken}}&name=Pixel%20Lead&email=pixel@example.com&source=website

### Lead capture: postback with form fields (expect 201 and the new lead)
POST {{api}}/inbound/postback?token={{inboundToken}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

name=Postback Lead&phone=%2B12025550123&amount=50&currency=USD
